#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Start the ready tickets of a "new flow" convoy (T04, af-gfyj6k).

Spec af-wf4w5r §0 rule 3 and §4, user story 82: code, not the Mayor, starts
the ready tickets of a convoy that carries the new-flow mark, in dependency
order and under the ceiling N, through bin/dispatch-door, which records each
start. A convoy without the mark is not touched: the Mayor advances it as
before.

    convoy-advance CONVOY        one pass on that convoy
    convoy-advance --all         one pass on every open marked convoy, and on
                                 those closed outside acceptance or abandon
    convoy-advance --check-only  exit 0 if such a convoy exists, else 1
    --stopped-ok                 with CONVOY or --all: exit 0, not 3, for a
                                 stopped convoy whose incident is raised

One pass starts every ticket of the convoy that is open, not yet started
through the door, and whose blockers are all closed, while a place is free
under N. N (`max_sessions` in config/delivery-flow.json) is the ceiling of
the authors, one setting for the whole Factory, shared between the Specs
(af-4xxlo7: the reviewer and the Evaluator have ceilings of their own,
`max_reviewer_sessions` and `max_evaluator_sessions`, applied by Gas City).
A place is taken by:

  - each live session of the author agent (config/delivery-roles.json),
    whatever the convoy;
  - each ticket of a marked convoy started through the door that no session
    has picked yet (still open): its author session is on its way.

A pass decides from the tracker alone, so a second pass on the same state
starts nothing more. Passes are serialised by a lock: two of them never
count the same free place.

A pass also merges (T18, af-gmz9s1; Spec §4): once the starts are made, it
hands each convoy that has a finished ticket to bin/spec-integration, which
merges one ticket into the integration branch of the Spec, runs the tests on
the merged result, and returns a ticket in conflict or red to its author. No
agent decides when a ticket is merged.

A pass settles no review of criterion tests (ADR-0030 L3; bin/test-review
removed in L7): the code review reads those tests after the green; a
gc.flow.test_review left on a ticket in flight is ignored.

A pass also raises a ticket bin/tdd-step stopped at its second amendment
(T45, af-7y457s; Spec §8): one request through bin/escalation-door that
names the ticket and « amendement épuisé », recorded by bin/convoy-state
stop-raised so that a later pass raises nothing more.

A pass also has the code of each finished ticket reviewed before its merge
(T14, af-96cusm; Spec §6, §8): it hands each convoy that has a finished
ticket not merged yet to bin/code-review settle, which sends the diff of the
ticket to a session of the reviewer role, sends it once more when the review
gave no result, stops the ticket when the relaunch gave none either, and
sends the answers given to its Blocking Findings to a second reviewer
session. bin/spec-integration merges nothing without a favorable verdict.
bin/code-review sends no reviewer on a branch that does not contain the tip
of the integration branch (T44, af-m1iibk; Spec §6): such a refusal is
listed under `code_review.behind` and does not fail the pass.

A pass also has each finished ticket evaluated on the launched product
before its merge (T15, af-higj9z; Spec §7, §8): it hands each convoy that
has a finished ticket not merged yet, or a launched product left to stop,
to bin/ticket-evaluation settle, which launches the product from a clean
copy of the ticket's commit, sends it to a session of the Evaluator role
(for a prefactoring: checks itself that the product starts), sends it once
more when the evaluation gave no result, stops the ticket when the relaunch
gave none either, parks a ticket whose criterion cannot be observed, and
stops the products once the states are in. Review and evaluation are sent
by the same pass: they run in parallel.

A pass also holds the correction rounds of a ticket (T17, af-rx0ocp;
Spec §8; bounds.correction_rounds, two since af-bv0ikr): once the code
review and the evaluation have both answered at the tip and one refused, it
hands the convoy to bin/correction-round settle, which sends everything both
refused to one fresh author session, opens the next round while one is
left, and stops the ticket still refused after its last round, raised once
to the operator.

A pass also closes the tickets (T19, af-iefuud; Spec §9): before the merge,
it hands each convoy that has a finished interface ticket whose fidelity was
not measured at its tip to bin/ticket-end fidelity, which runs the
mechanical fidelity check on the screens of its Validated Prototype; after
the merge, it hands each convoy that has a merged ticket still open to
bin/ticket-end settle, which closes the ticket once the nine conditions of
the ticket-end gate are met and leaves it open, with what is missing named,
otherwise. No agent closes a ticket of a marked convoy.

A pass also counts and bounds the resumes of a ticket (T20, af-y9pw9z; Spec
§5, §8): a ticket whose author session was interrupted (by its Ticket Exit,
or ended without one), that the merge returned, whose repair is closed or
whose request was answered is sent to one fresh author session on the same
branch, through bin/dispatch-door, and the resume is counted
(bin/convoy-state open-resume). So is a finished, unmerged ticket whose
branch does not contain the tip of the integration branch (cause `behind`,
T44: `behind` of bin/code-review show), once per Ticket Exit, and recorded
even when the ceiling makes its session wait: its exit is taken back, so
neither the review nor the evaluation is sent on the old tip. That resume
comes from the factory (another ticket merged), so K does not count it,
once per tip of the integration branch; a second one on a tip already
resumed for is counted (af-npz9v1.36, docs/CONVOY_ADVANCE.md). So is a ticket
stopped because its Ticket Evaluation gave no result (af-xhc0sj), once per
tip of the integration branch: the resume lifts the stop, keeps it on the
resume, and withdraws its request; so is a ticket stopped at its second
amendment once the operator answered « a » to its request (af-25o7vr,
cause `amendment_granted`, one amendment more), or whose every change
since the freeze is the base's it merged (af-npz9v1.39, cause
`inherited_change`, no answer asked), or a repair that only moves a proof
stopped all green before bin/tdd-step gave it its path (af-oa2ci4, cause
`proof_moved`, no answer asked, once per stop), or a ticket stopped all
green by a red that ran each test once, before bin/tdd-step replayed a pass
up to k runs (af-batj8g, cause `red_replayed`, no answer asked, once per
stop); every other stop stays
with the operator. At the
last resume of a same cause (bounds.resumes, one bound per cause, ADR-0030
L2: these causes and a commit after a verdict; the correction rounds keep
their own bound, bounds.correction_rounds), the ticket is
parked with every ticket that waits for it and is not restarted; the others
keep starting. When nothing but parked tickets is left in a convoy, the pass
raises one request for the convoy, on a bead of its own, through
bin/escalation-door: it names each parked ticket and its cause. The answer
of the operator that lifts a parking is read by the pass, which lifts it
(bin/convoy-state lift-park): the ticket and those behind it are startable
again, with no hand on a ticket.

A pass also holds the two stops of a convoy (T21, af-cbp84n; Spec §8, user
story 53). While its integration branch is red (bin/convoy-state:
`integration_red`, written by bin/spec-integration, which then refuses every
merge), the pass starts no ticket and sends no resume; it publishes one
`repair` for that red, through the patch door (bin/ticket-graph-publish
bd-patch), which names the control that is red, and records it on the red
(bin/convoy-state set-integration-repair): one repair per red, whatever the
number of passes. That repair is the one ticket the pass starts and
bin/spec-integration merges. Once the control is green again
bin/spec-integration withdraws the red, and the starts and the merges go on
with no hand on the convoy. While as many Planning Exceptions as the bound
allows (`bounds.open_planning_exceptions` of config/delivery-flow.json, 2)
are open on the Spec of the convoy, the pass starts no new ticket; the
tickets at work go on, resumes included. An exception answered by the
operator is no longer open: the next pass starts again.

A convoy in an "état sans règle" (bin/convoy-state: a ticket started or
closed outside its door, evidence or a counter that cannot be read) is
stopped (T34, af-ckwina; Spec §0 rule 5): the pass starts none of its
tickets, writes none of them, and raises one factory incident, a bead of its
own that bin/escalation-door puts on the operator's list, naming the ticket
and the reason. The incident is recorded on the convoy through
bin/convoy-state, so the next passes on the same anomalies raise nothing
more. Once the state is valid again the pass withdraws the incident, closes
its bead and starts the ready tickets: no agent resumes the convoy.

A marked convoy does not close by itself (T22, af-kn83no; Spec §9): it is
closed only by code, on the operator's words. One found closed any other way
(bin/convoy-state list, `closed_outside`) is such an "état sans règle": the
pass walks it too, starts nothing in it and raises the same factory incident,
withdrawn once the convoy is open again.

A pass also runs the end-of-Spec gate (T23, af-s5uysn; Spec §9, points 1 to
3): once every ticket of the convoy is closed and its integration branch is
not red, it hands the convoy to bin/spec-end run, which renders three
mechanical verdicts -- registry, tests, fidelity -- on one tip of the
integration branch, the protected branch taken up. A condition that is not
met is an outcome of the pass: the registry names the element (and asks the
operator, once, about a deviation or a « non fait » left without a final
state); red tests or a red fidelity are the red of the integration branch,
with one round of the end counted, whose one `repair` the next pass
publishes as above. When the operator answered that an element is to be
repaired, the pass publishes that repair too and names it on the element
(bin/convoy-state set-item-repair).

A pass also has the assembled product evaluated (T24, af-oy7v3i; Spec §7,
§9, points 4 and 5): once the gate has rendered its three mechanical
verdicts green on a commit, it hands the convoy to bin/outcome-evaluation
settle, which launches the product from a clean copy of that commit, sends
it to a session of the Evaluator role, sends it once more when the
evaluation gave no result, stops it when the relaunch gave none either, and
stops the products nothing runs on any more. What the Evaluator of the end
drafted is published by the pass, through the patch door, once its states
are in: one `repair` per user story it did not observe, and one per finding
« hors ticket » it classified « repaired », each named where it was drafted
(bin/convoy-state set-outcome-repair). Such a repair starts, merges and
closes like any ticket; the gate then renders its verdicts on the new tip
and the product is evaluated again. A draft the patch door refuses is
recorded where it was drafted, with the reason (set-outcome-repair
--refused), never published again, and stops the Outcome Evaluation at the
commit of its last round (`outcome_repair_refused`): bin/outcome-evaluation
raises that stop once to the operator.
In the same pass, on the commit of those three verdicts, it has the whole
assembled diff of the Spec reviewed (T25, af-ji2ruy; Spec §6 « Fin de
Spec », §9 point 4), through bin/spec-end-review settle: one reviewer
session, one relaunch, then the stop of the review. The gate reads that
review as its sixth condition. Each Blocking Finding comes with the
`repair` its reviewer drafted: the pass publishes it through the patch door
as any added ticket and names it on the finding (bin/convoy-state
set-end-review-repair); merged, it moves the tip and the review is made
again in full.
Last, once the six conditions before it are met on that commit and the gate
refuses on its seventh alone, the pass has the Evidence Pack generated by
code (T27, af-r43we4; Spec §10, §9 point 6), through bin/evidence-pack
generate, and runs the gate again in the same pass.

Once Benjamin answered « accepté » or « abandonné » (bin/owner-answer), the
pass follows his answer through bin/outcome-promote run (T30, af-vlzc6v;
Spec §9 and §11) and renders nothing else on that Outcome: the one merge of
the integration branch into the protected branch and the closing of the
convoy on his words, or the closing alone (`promotion`). When the protected
branch moved since his judgement and the mechanical controls replayed on
its take-up are red, or the two branches conflict, nothing is merged: his
acceptance is voided, the same pass publishes the one `repair` of that red,
and the convoy goes back through the end of its Spec to a new Acceptance
Request. A convoy closed by these commands is no longer walked by --all;
named as CONVOY, the pass starts nothing in it and only has the closing of
its Spec and its draft replayed.

Every answer is one JSON object on stdout. Exit status: 0 the pass is done
(what it started is listed, possibly nothing); 1 refused or could not run,
the dispatch door refused a ticket (named under `refused`), an incident
or a grouped request could not be raised or withdrawn, a resume could not
be sent, a repair could not be published, or the merge pass or the settlement of
the test reviews, of the code reviews, of the evaluations, of the
correction rounds, of the fidelity checks, of the ticket-end gate or of the
end-of-Spec gate or of the Outcome Evaluation could not run, or the merge
or the closing that follows the operator's answer could not be made; 3 a
convoy is in an "état sans règle": nothing of it is started (0 with
--stopped-ok once its incident is raised: what the order runs, so that a
stopped convoy is not also an order failure);
4 the convoy does not carry the mark: nothing is started, nothing is written;
75 every failure of the pass is an explicit capacity deferral (`NOT RUN,
exit 75`): nothing is accepted, and the next order pass retries without a
chronic-failure alert.
Settings, reads and the order that runs it: docs/CONVOY_ADVANCE.md.
"""

